   Wat je gaat doen As a Football Logistics Worker, you help prepare football clothing and products for customers and fans. You will work with different products and tasks, so no day has to be exactly the same.

Your tasks can include:
- Picking football clothing and products;
- Packing orders;
- Printing names and numbers on football shirts;
- Checking products and orders;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Sorting clothing and products;
- Keeping your workplace clean and organized;
- Helping with other warehouse tasks when needed.

Working hours are 8:00–17:00, with up to 2 hours of overtime if requested in advance.
 Wat we je bieden At UPS, you get good employment conditions and clear agreements.
- Up to €18.75 gross per hour including shift allowance;
- Starting salary of €15.00 gross per hour;
- Around 40 hours per week;
- Possible shift allowances depending on your working hours;
- 25 vacation days;
- 8% holiday allowance;
- Travel allowance up to €9.47 net per working day;
- No previous warehouse experience required;
- Training and support from day one;
- Possibility to stay longer after the initial period;
- Opportunities to move to other positions within UPS.

At Start People, we operate on the principle of equal pay; your terms and conditions of employment always match those of colleagues who are employed directly by the client. This means that, in addition to your hourly rate, your terms and conditions of employment also include, for example, the number of days off, allowances, time-off-in-lieu payments and other pay components.
